  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BRIDGE: Bridging Communities to Protect Human Rights and Fundamental Freedoms</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overall Objective: &lt;/strong&gt;To create a conducive environment in which human rights and fundamental freedoms, of women, youth and marginalized communities, are respected and protected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific Objective: &lt;/strong&gt;To enable and empower 200 women and youth (CSO&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;political) leaders, and 100 Human Rights Defenders (HRDs) and build solidarity amongst 15 people&#xbf;s forums to promote peaceful, inclusive, and resilient communities&amp;nbsp;in&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;5 districts in Northern Sri Lanka.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outcome 1:&lt;/strong&gt; To enhance support and deepen engagement with 200 women and youth leaders and 100 HRDs to facilitate and lead political and economic transformation and challenge the structural constraints that exclude women and youth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outcome 2: &lt;/strong&gt;To promote collective action and solidarity, improve access to legal and other support services for women and youth leaders and HRDs and promote awareness and appreciation of human rights including gender equality through digital innovation and responsible social media access and use.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
